+    \item \textbf{Scale and durability.} Scale is measured to $10^5$ triples using full snapshots. Larger or distributed deployments would require a persistent delta/Merkle design and stronger durability/failure models; the reported transaction tests are local, not distributed consensus or storage-device durability tests.
+    \item \textbf{Novelty boundary.} Truth maintenance, provenance, argumentation, dependency invalidation and predecessor-anchored activation already exist \cite{doyle1979tms,buneman2001provenance,dung1995acceptability,feldman1979make,he2026continuity}. Support sets are a restricted declared fragment, not an advance on ATMS or Boolean provenance. The claimed contribution is the research-specific composition, operational boundary and registration-aware evaluation, and no universal claim is made over unsurveyed event-sourcing, data-versioning or ML-lineage systems.
